# Git branch naming

Never use the `cursor/` prefix when creating or suggesting branch names.

Use standard git-flow prefixes, then a concise hyphen-separated description:

| Prefix | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `feature/` | New functionality |
| `fix/` | Bug fixes |
| `refactor/` | Restructuring without behavior change |
| `docs/` | Documentation only |
| `chore/` | Tooling, CI, deps, housekeeping |

Examples:
- `feature/methylation-matrix-preflight` (not `cursor/methylation-matrix-preflight`)
- `fix/ukb-eid-join-audit`
- `chore/pre-commit-hooks`
